---
import CouchpilotLayout from '../../layouts/CouchpilotLayout.astro';
const h2 = 'text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6';
---

<CouchpilotLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Support | Couchpilot"
  description="Help for the Couchpilot app: contact, deleting your data, where the data comes from and how to cancel Couchpilot Pro."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 max-w-4xl text-slate-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">SUPPORT</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        Something not working, or an idea? Write to
        <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="cp-accent">info@endure-cycling.com</a>. Tell us your device,
        the app version (bottom of your profile) and what you did, and we'll get back to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>How do I delete my data?</h2>
      <p>
        Open your profile and tap “Delete all my data”. This removes everything from your device and deletes your user ID
        and all its data on our server, with or without an account. You can also ask us by email.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Where does the data come from?</h2>
      <p>
        Titles, people, genres and critic scores come from Wikidata, descriptions from Wikipedia, posters, user ratings
        and trending lists from Trakt, and streaming availability and the top 10 lists from the Streaming Availability
        API by Movie of the Night. Couchpilot uses Trakt but is not endorsed or certified by Trakt.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Why does a title say “not checked yet”?</h2>
      <p>
        Our catalog has around 200,000 films and series. Where each one streams is checked step by step, the most popular
        titles first. When you open a title we have not checked yet, the app checks it right away. On busy days the
        daily limit for these checks can be reached; then try again later.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>A provider or price is wrong</h2>
      <p>
        Streaming catalogs change daily, and we update them every day. If something is still wrong after a day, send us
        the title and your country.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>How do I cancel Couchpilot Pro?</h2>
      <p>
        Pro is a subscription in the App Store or Google Play, so you cancel it there: on iPhone in Settings › your name ›
        Subscriptions, on Android in the Play Store › profile › Payments &amp; subscriptions › Subscriptions. Deleting the
        app does not cancel the subscription.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Read our <a href="/couchpilot/privacy/" class="cp-accent">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</CouchpilotLayout>
